{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAGBWqnyNKVsYaCB8B9x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted **index 1 (Sb fraction 0.181)** as the best composition. It had the highest EQE I measured, **0.956%**. All 5 EQE measurements are used, and I used 3 of the 5 XRD measurements.\n\nEQE rises steeply as the film gets richer in Fe:\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 19 | 0.681 | −0.003 |\n| 12 | 0.511 | 0.00005 |\n| 6 | 0.296 | 0.099 |\n| 2 | 0.199 | 0.779 |\n| 1 | 0.181 | **0.956** |\n\nI didn't measure the EQE of index 0 (Sb 0.161), the only composition more Fe-rich than index 1. If the trend keeps going, it could be the true best on the line. I picked index 1 for the last measurement as a hedge: it wins if the trend continues or if EQE peaks near 0.2 Sb. XRD shows index 0 has a different set of phases from indexes 2 and 4, so its EQE can't be predicted reliably from their trend.\n\nMy reading of the XRD is tentative. I think most peaks come from the Pt substrate. The rest look like an FeSbO₄-like rutile phase that grows as Sb increases, plus possibly hematite (Fe₂O₃). That fits with Fe-rich films performing better, but I didn't use the XRD to decide anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":569,"cache_read_input_tokens":7465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":569},"output_tokens":480,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4cd07717-b110-4ea5-bdfb-e8cc2aad6546","uuid":"39f340fc-d6dc-483b-8586-60fb8093a29b","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:19:56.031Z","request_id":"req_011CfAGBWKnezsf6PGocNFaU"}
